# HB-SAMPLE (CROSS-PORT, owner 2026-10-11): Goku's forward throw is Mewtwo's ThrowF, numbers read from retail Mewtwo in this engine (tools/lua throw_probe.lua).
# Mewtwo holds the victim in front, releases a 5% hit at script frame 19, then fires five small shadow balls (script frames 33 40 47 54 61, 7 apart, speed 6.0, 45 frames
# alive, about 0.9% each); his throw ends at frame 75. Here the balls are Goku's ki blasts (article KiThrow, index 5; homing instead of Mewtwo's arm-pose aim).
# Throw slot 0 = Mewtwo's: damage 5, angle 78, KBG 100, fixed knockback 38, base 0; slot 1 = his second slot: damage 3, angle 361, KBG 100, base 40.
# Not XV2 data: the clip is the ki blast pose ATC_SHOT_F retimed to Mewtwo's 75 frames. Ledger: HB-SAMPLE, a starting point the owner edits in the Workbench.
PUT ANIM_RATE 1.0
wait 1
throw idx=0 damage=5 unk0=78 hit_x24=100 hit_x28=38 hit_x2C=0
throw idx=1 damage=3 unk0=361 hit_x24=100 hit_x28=0 hit_x2C=40
wait_until 19
throw_flag hit_idx=0
clear_hitboxes
wait_until 33
CALL geno.article.spawn 5
wait_until 40
CALL geno.article.spawn 5
wait_until 47
CALL geno.article.spawn 5
wait_until 54
CALL geno.article.spawn 5
wait_until 61
CALL geno.article.spawn 5
wait_until 74
iasa
